      "verdict": "true_positive",
      "reason": "Arbiter ruling (Fable, upheld on review): the floating then() at line 27 returns a promise that rejects if any listener throws, and CancelToken.subscribe is public API, so a user listener's error becomes an unhandled rejection that also skips the remaining cancel listeners.",
      "labeller": "human:operator",
      "checks": [
        {
          "source": "model:claude-fable-5-1",
          "verdict": "true_positive",
          "reason": "Line 27 calls the native `this.promise.then(cb)` (the override comes later, at line 39) and discards the derived promise with no catch; the source promise can never reject, but the derived one rejects if `token._listeners[i](cancel)` at line 33 throws, and because `subscribe()` is public API (index.d.ts:603) that listener can be user code, so the throw becomes an unhandled rejection and the loop stops before the remaining listeners run."
        },
        {
          "source": "model:claude-sonnet-5-5",
          "verdict": "true_positive",
          "reason": "`this.promise.then((cancel) => {...})` at line 27 is a floating promise with no catch, so a throwing listener in the callback would produce an unhandled rejection."
        }
      ]
